0.5 \\%$ of the speed of sound in air. The frequency of the reflected sound received at the engine is","options":["$0.990 \\mathrm{f}$","$0.995 \\mathrm{f}$","$1.005 \\mathrm{f}$","$1.010 \\mathrm{f}$"],"answer":0,"solution":"$f_{1}=f_{0}\\left[\\frac{v}{v+v_{s}}\\right]f_{R}=f_{1}\\left[\\frac{v-v_{s}}{v}\\right]=f_{0}\\left[\\frac{v-v_{s}}{v+v_{s}}\\right]=\\left[1-\\frac{2 v_{s}}{v}\\right] f=0.990 f$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2013 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d2133aecdbb75b5ff0cf"},{"id":52577,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Waves and Sound","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"A whistle emitting a loud sound of frequency $540 \\mathrm{~Hz}$ is whirled in a horizontal circle of radius $2 \\mathrm{~m}$ and at a constant angular speed of $15 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}$. The speed of sound is $330 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$. The ratio of the highest to the lowest frequency heard by a listener standing at rest at a large distance from the center of the circle is :","options":["$1.0$","$1.1$","$1.2$","$1.4$"],"answer":2,"solution":"<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FrwVljqIfhsdMjguj6Fhtnvv-x5Q8RVVU5zNKQ8UP-NA.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FrwVljqIfhsdMjguj6Fhtnvv-x5Q8RVVU5zNKQ8UP-NA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FrwVljqIfhsdMjguj6Fhtnvv-x5Q8RVVU5zNKQ8UP-NA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>\n$n^{\\prime}=n\\left[\\frac{v-0}{v+v_{s}}\\right]n \"=n\\left[\\frac{v}{v+v_{s}}\\right]\\frac{n^{\\prime}}{n^{\\prime \\prime}}=\\frac{v-v_{s}}{v+v_{s}}\\frac{n^{\\prime}}{n^{\\prime \\prime}}=\\frac{v+v_{s}}{v-v_{s}}=\\frac{330+30}{330-30}=\\frac{360}{300}=1.2$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2014 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d21350c190e03369ff8d"},{"id":52578,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Waves and Sound","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"A transverse wave of frequency $500 \\mathrm{~Hz}$ and speed $100 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ is traveling in the positive $\\mathrm{x}$ direction on a long string. At time $\\mathrm{t}=0 \\mathrm{~s}$ the displacements at $x=0.0 \\mathrm{~m}$ and at $\\mathrm{x}=0.25 \\mathrm{~m}$ are $0.0 \\mathrm{~m}$ and $0.02 \\mathrm{~m}$, respectively. The displacement at $\\mathrm{x}=0.2 \\mathrm{~m}$ at $\\mathrm{t}=5 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~s}$ is","options":["$-0.04 \\mathrm{~m}$","$-0.02 \\mathrm{~m}$","$0.04 \\mathrm{~m}$","$0.02 \\mathrm{~m}$"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\mathrm{y}=\\mathrm{A} \\sin (\\mathrm{kx}-\\omega \\mathrm{t})$\nat $\\mathrm{x}=0.025, \\mathrm{y}=0.02\\mathrm{v}=\\mathrm{v} \\lambda\\lambda=\\frac{100}{500}=\\frac{1}{5} \\mathrm{~m}\\mathrm{y}=0.02=\\mathrm{A} \\sin \\left(\\frac{2 \\pi}{\\lambda} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\mathrm{y}=0.002=\\mathrm{A} \\sin \\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{2}\\right)\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{A}=0.02 \\mathrm{~m}\\therefore \\mathrm{y}=0.02 \\sin (\\mathrm{kx}-\\omega \\mathrm{t})\\quad=0.02 \\sin \\left(10 \\pi \\times 0.2-1000 \\pi \\times 5 \\times 10^{-4}\\right]\\quad=0.02 \\sin [2 \\pi-0.5 \\pi]\\quad=0.02 \\sin \\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right)=-0.02 \\mathrm{~m}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2017 (5 Nov SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213a76d6368742ae674"}]}